  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Authority, not a second engine",
      "items": [
        "Gateway owns registry, grants, operation correlation, task reservations, durable CLI-routing permits and connection generations. Observations are dated caches; results are not persisted.",
        "Connector owns local alias \u2192 pinned root/project mapping and its stricter ceiling. Effective permission is the intersection.",
        "Delegate alone owns admission/refusal, creation, launch, supervision, cancellation and accepted outcomes. Local CLI/SSH/TUI share this authority.",
        "CLI-routing permits survive lost replies and Gateway restart. Only actual CLI cleanup or a fenced same-process complete census releases them; a changed connector process needs local-admin CLI-only drain attestation. Delegate task reservations remain separate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust and transport",
      "items": [
        "OAuth authenticates every MCP call; no user mTLS certificate or token forwarding. Gateway is trusted and sees plaintext; end-to-end encryption is deferred.",
        "Devices initiate WSS. Sessions carry generation-bound requests and responses. Same device account is one trust boundary; project grants are routing, not OS sandboxing.",
        "Only public installed Delegate CLI; no shell, provider adapter, private task-file access, executor queue or automatic failover."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Planning source and implementation gate",
      "items": [
        "Source: approved implementation contract v7, OWNERS / COMPONENTS; DELEGATE PUBLIC PREREQUISITE; IDENTITY / ENROLLMENT / DEVICE TRANSPORT.",
        "This is a target design, not source-backed implementation evidence. Proposed connector commands require a separately reviewed Delegate change in its dedicated worktree, using its own harness.",
        "Before PR: independent integrated review and no known unresolved P0/P1/P2. Plan approval is not cloud acceptance or release readiness."
      ]
    }
  ]
